Package: emphasis
Type: Package
Title: Monte Carlo Inference for Phylogenetic Diversification Models
Version: 1.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Francisco", "Richter", email = "franciscorichter@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Thijs", "Janzen", role = "ctb",
           comment = "earlier C++ implementation"),
    person("Hanno", "Hildenbrandt", role = "ctb",
           comment = "earlier C++ implementation"))
Description: Fits birth-death models of species diversification in which the
    speciation and extinction rates depend on covariates generated by the
    process itself, such as the number of lineages, the age structure of the
    lineages and their evolutionary distinctiveness, to reconstructed
    phylogenies that contain only extant species. The likelihood is
    integrated over the unobserved extinct lineages by importance sampling
    on augmented trees, and the parameters are estimated by Monte Carlo
    expectation-maximization, by the cross-entropy method, or from a
    generalized additive model fitted to a simulated likelihood surface,
    following Richter, Haegeman, Etienne and Wit (2020)
    <doi:10.1111/stan.12205>. Trees can be simulated under the same models,
    and incomplete taxon sampling is supported.
